msgstr "Project-Id-Version: ydotool\nReport-Msgid-Bugs-To: anton@sirius.if.ua\nPOT-Creation-Date: 2026-11-06 02:48+0700\nPO-Revision-Date: 2026-11-06 00:00+0000\nLast-Translator: ydotool translation tooling <anton@sirius.if.ua>\nLanguage-Team: oc\nLanguage: oc\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\nPlural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);\nX-Native-Review: pending\n"

msgid "Usage: click [OPTION]... [BUTTONS]...\nClick mouse buttons.\n\nOptions:\n  -r, --repeat=N             Repeat entire sequence N times\n  -D, --next-delay=N         Delay N milliseconds between input events (up/down,                                a complete click means doubled time)\n  -P, --press-release        Press & release mouse button to complete a click, (optional)\n  -h, --help                 Display this help and exit\n\nHow to specify buttons:\n  Now all mouse buttons are represented using hexadecimal numeric values, with an optional\nbit mask to specify if mouse up/down needs to be omitted.\n  0x00 - LEFT\n  0x01 - RIGHT\n  0x02 - MIDDLE\n  0x03 - SIDE\n  0x04 - EXTR\n  0x05 - FORWARD\n  0x06 - BACK\n  0x07 - TASK\n  0x40 - Mouse down\n  0x80 - Mouse up\n  Examples:\n    0x00: chooses left button, but does nothing (you can use this to implement extra sleeps)\n    0xC0: left button click (down then up)\n    0x41: right button down\n    0x82: middle button up\n  The '0x' prefix can be omitted if you want.\n"
msgstr "Usatge: click [OPTION]... [BUTTONS]...\nClicatz los botons de la mirga.\n\nOpcions:\n  -r, --repeat=N             Repetir tota la sequéncia N còps\n  -D, --next-delay=N         Espèra N millisegondas entre los eveniments d’entrada (pujada/baissada,                                un clic complet compta lo doble)\n  -P, --press-release        Plegar e relargar lo boton de la mirga per acabar un clic (opcional)\n  -h, --help                 Afichar aquesta ajuda e sortir\n\nCossí indicar los botons:\n  Ara totes los botons de la mirga son representats per de valors numerics exadecimals, amb una mascara binària opcional per indicar se cal ometre la pujada o la baissada del boton.\n  0x00 - LEFT (ESQUÈRRE)\n  0x01 - RIGHT (DRECH)\n  0x02 - MIDDLE (MÈDI)\n  0x03 - SIDE (COSTAT)\n  0x04 - EXTR (EXTÈR)\n  0x05 - FORWARD (AVANT)\n  0x06 - BACK (ARRIÈR)\n  0x07 - TASK (TASCAS)\n  0x40 - Boton de la mirga baissat\n  0x80 - Boton de la mirga levat\n  Exemples:\n    0x00: selecciona lo boton esquèrre, mas fa pas res (podètz l’utilizar per apondre de pausas)\n    0xC0: clic del boton esquèrre (baissada puèi pujada)\n    0x41: boton drech baissat\n    0x82: boton mièg levat\n  Lo prefixe '0x' pòt èsser omés.\n"

